From 5a367adffa843d787449fe88fccd20d698234840 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Bloomin <452472+daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:00:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): declare paused_for_update on
 MessageCompletePayload [daveey]

update_pause.announce_pause (cc29d783ed) deliberately stamps paused_for_update=True on the
terminal message.complete frame of a turn paused at a step boundary for a core update, but the
contract model forbade the extra key, so every paused turn's terminal frame logged
'violates its wire contract ... extra_forbidden' (agent.log, 2026-10-28 22:17:41 PDT).

Declare it as an optional bool and regenerate the shared gateway contract files.

Why the tests missed it: the turn_env fixture replaced server._emit with a bare recorder, so
no frame in test_update_pause.py ever reached the strict contract check. The fixture now runs
check_payload on every frame; added a direct announce_pause -> MessageCompletePayload test,
an ordinary-stop control (no pause flag, no watcher) and a generated-TS field check.
